      {
        "tipo": "intro",
        "min": 3,
        "texto": "Imagine that you arrive on a street in Paris on a sunny morning. Two people meet and greet each other. Before any rule, you will listen to this scene. Then you will repeat it. This is how a language is learned: first the ear, then the explanation. You already know a lot of French: «restaurant», «menu», «hôtel», «café», «croissant», «boutique», «bonjour». Next to each new word there is an approximate pronunciation in English-style respelling. The «ew» is the French «u»: lips rounded as for «oo», tongue as for «ee». The «uh» is the sound of «eu». The «ahn», the «ohn» and the «an» are nasal vowels. This help does not replace the audio: always listen before you repeat."
